            <ArticleTitle>Reduced movement of median nerve in carpal tunnel during wrist flexion in patients with non-specific arm pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>217-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Magnetic resonance scans on patients with non-specific arm pain (repetitive strain injury) show reduced median-nerve movement in the carpal tunnel, suggesting that this common condition may involve nerve entrapment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
